{% doc %}
  @prompt
    Act as an expert Shopify backend and frontend Liquid/CSS developer. Build a fully responsive, pixel-perfect custom Shopify section that 100% replicates the copy, visual hierarchy, layouts, and components from the image "image_b642a2.jpg".
    
    ### 1. Global Theme Integration & Base Styles
    - **Inherited Styles:** The section MUST use the existing Shopify theme's font family variables (e.g., `var(--font-heading-family)` and `var(--font-body-family)`), its standard maximum section width (e.g., matching `.page-width` or `.container`), and default responsive side padding.
    - **Section Layout:** On desktop, this section is split into a 2-column layout (Left Column: content and light grid cards; Right Column: a large dark summary card). On mobile, columns stack vertically into a single column.
    - **Background:** Clean white background (#FFFFFF).
    
    ### 2. Left Column Layout & Content
    - **Eyebrow Badge:** A small, light gray rounded rectangle badge with subtle padding. Text reads: "PROOF // CUSTOMER RESULTS" in small uppercase letters.
    - **Main Heading:** "PROVEN RETAIL OUTCOMES." in large, bold, dark navy capitalized lettering.
    - **Subheading:** "Real Results from Flow Deployments Across Japan." in a slightly smaller, bold navy font.
    - **Body Paragraph:** Muted, comfortable line-height text reading: "Flow customers achieve measurable improvements in conversion, staffing efficiency, VMD performance, and operational execution. Each case study documents deployment scope, implementation approach, and verified business outcomes."
    - **Mini 2x2 White Grid Cards:** Below the paragraph, a 2-column grid of small white cards with soft rounded corners (~8px) and subtle borders or soft drop shadows:
      - **Card 1:** Stat: "500+" (bold dark navy) | Label: "Active Stores" (small gray subtext)
      - **Card 2:** Stat: "50+" (bold dark navy) | Label: "Retail Brands" (small gray subtext)
      - **Card 3:** Stat: "98.5%" (bold dark navy) | Label: "Measurement Accuracy" (small gray subtext)
      - **Card 4:** Stat: "99.9%" (bold dark navy) | Label: "Platform Uptime" (small gray subtext)
    
    ### 3. Right Column Layout & Content (Large Dark Card)
    - **Container Box:** A solid deep navy blue container block (#0E2A3A or similar) with smooth rounded corners (~16px) and interior padding.
    - **Inner Header Elements:**
      - **Badge:** A small, dark green/olive background badge with uppercase white text: "AGGREGATE IMPACT".
      - **Heading:** "Measured Results Across Deployments" in bold white text.
      - **Subtext:** Soft, light-gray text reading: "Representative outcomes from Flow customers in fashion, lifestyle, and specialty retail."
    - **Hero Metric Card (Full-Width Inside Dark Card):**
      - Background: A slightly lighter, semi-transparent navy or desaturated dark-blue tone with rounded corners.
      - Layout: Left side contains text; right side features a small, muted olive square badge with a thin green line-graph trend icon pointing up and right.
      - Label: "SALES GROWTH (YoY)" in small gray capital letters.
      - Big Stat: "108.9%" in very large bold white text.
      - Subtext: "2024 aggregate across Flow customers" in small gray text.
    - **Nested 2x2 Metric Grid:** Below the hero card, create a 2-column layout for 4 smaller data blocks (each matching the hero card's background and rounded corners):
      - **Block 1:** Title: "CONVERSION LIFT" (small caps) | Stat: "+8.93%" (bold white) | Detail: "Major retailer (220 stores)" (small gray text)
      - **Block 2:** Title: "ROI MULTIPLE" (small caps) | Stat: "50x" (bold white) | Detail: "National fashion chain" (small gray text)
      - **Block 3:** Title: "CAPTURE RATE" (small caps) | Stat: "+23.9%" (bold white) | Detail: "Multi-brand operator" (small gray text)
      - **Block 4:** Title: "SALES INCREASE" (small caps) | Stat: "+25%" (bold white) | Detail: "Stores using dashboard" (small gray text)
    - **Footer Text:** Placed at the very bottom of the dark container card, centered or left-aligned in a small, soft light-gray font size: "Results from documented case studies. Individual outcomes vary based on deployment scope, store operations, and market conditions."
    
    ### 4. Shopify Code Requirements
    - Write self-contained CSS (scoped to the section ID) to prevent layout bleeding. 
    - Use modern CSS Grid or Flexbox to guarantee flawless responsiveness from a full desktop display down to tight mobile screens.
    - Implement a clean Shopify theme schema with editable text inputs for all headings, subheadings, metrics, and labels so that the section remains fully dynamic in the Shopify Theme Editor.
{% enddoc %}
{% assign ai_gen_id = block.id | replace: '_', '' | downcase %}

